# Fixture script-check registry for tests/suites/report.sh's COMPLIANCE-04
# case (the CIS compliance view in report.md/report.html).  NOT a shipped
# catalog: modules/cloud/aws/live/checks.rules owns the real `CLOUD-S3-*` ids
# for real.  Mirrors the shape tests/fixtures/checks-registry/modules/dast/
# checks.rules already documents for the OWASP compliance test - a small,
# fully-controlled registry so the four-way honesty split (findings/clean/
# not-applicable/filtered, plus out-of-scope for a real id no fixture check
# cites at all) is deterministic, rather than coupled to however many real
# `cis:` mappings modules/cloud/ happens to carry today.
#
# EVERY ID HERE IS DELIBERATELY DISTINCT FROM EVERY SHIPPED ONE (see the DAST
# fixture's own header for why: E019 scopes check-id uniqueness to the whole
# repository, not to one file).  The `cis:` VALUES are real CIS AWS
# Foundations Benchmark v3.0.0 ids from the shipped data/cis-mappings table
# (rules/RULE-FORMAT.md §9.1.1a: that namespace is never cross-referenced
# against a `cis:` field either direction, so reusing a real id here is not a
# collision) - that is what lets this fixture prove real labels and the real
# benchmark version render, rather than only the "unknown id" degrade path.

id: CLOUD-S3-CIS_FIXTURE_PUBLIC-01
title: Fixture public-exposure check (findings bucket)
script: aws/live/s3.sh
severity: high
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-732
owasp: A01:2021
tags: config-read
tags: quick
tags: compliance
coverage-scope: account-region
cis: 2.1.4
remediation: This is a fixture check; it exists only to prove the CIS
  compliance view groups a live finding under its control id.
references: CWE-732

